text:
Maria L.: heads up — noticed tail latency increase on /chat-stream when kv reuse dips. can we add a per-route reuse heatmap + token-level latency breakdown to the token-latency dashboard? want to correlate evictions -> kernel selection changes.

Ashok: yes. early hypothesis: kernel selector flips to slower matmul path when seq_len > 1024 after eviction bursts. also batching efficiency drops if KV lookups serialize. need a metric for active kernel variant per node.

Henry P.: ran a quick profile on the noisy window this morning. minimal list of metrics to add:

```
kv.cache.hit_rate{route}
kv.cache.evictions{route,shard}
kv.cache.reuse_ratio{route,shard}
runtime.kernel.variant{node,model}
runtime.batch.size.dist{route}
token.latency.p50/p95/p99{route,phase=kv_lookup|compute|generation}
kv.cache.reuse_by_route_heatmap{route,minute_bin}
```

The heatmap should be minute-binned and show reuse fraction on y, route on x (or the other way around depending on panel).

Samir K.: can infra expose `runtime.kernel.variant` as a tag? atm it's only an internal label in the runtime logs. would help us see if specific kernels correlate with higher p99.

InfraBot: datadog-scraper v2 deployed to staging — will scrape `runtime.kernel.variant` and `kv.cache.reuse_ratio` for 24h. :rocket:

Maria L.: perfect. also want per-route stacked barbreakdown for token latency phases (kv_lookup / compute / generation) so we can see where most of the tail is. i'll add an alert rule: if reuse_rate < 0.6 AND token.latency.p99{route="/chat-stream"} > 800ms then notify #incidents and runtime-oncall.

Ashok: i'll draft the dashboard JSON and a short exporter patch to emit `runtime.kernel.variant` as a metric tag. ETA EOD. will include an example graph: heatmap + p99 overlay + evictions timeseries.

Henry P.: tiny UX note — use log scale for evictions axis, linear hides short sharp spikes that cause immediate evictions. also add an annotation stream for autoscaler events and model rollouts so we can correlate.

Samir K.: ping me before merging, i'll run a route-specific replay for /chat-stream at different seq lengths and check reuse_by_route_heatmap. happy to validate alerts.

Maria L.: sweet. thanks all. once InfraBot finishes the 24h scrape we'll pick a stable 6h window to baseline and then iterate. :thumbsup:
